sasha (DevEx): Heads-up — Node quickstart example in README breaks when you copy/paste into a file and run with node >=18. Using `await` at top level without ESM/toplevel-await causes a SyntaxError.

sasha (DevEx): Repro: create index.js with the snippet below and run `node index.js`
```js
import { Redwood } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood();
const resp = await client.generate({ model: 'rw1' });
console.log(resp);
```

sasha (DevEx): Error you get: `SyntaxError: await is only valid in async function` (or node complains about requiring --experimental-top-level-await in older versions). Also noticed the README uses a literal `MY_API_KEY` in the example rather than `process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY` which encourages copy/paste secrets. :facepalm:

liam (eng): Oof. Can you file a quick PR? This will confuse new users.

sasha (DevEx): Yep, opened a small PR that fixes the example to use an async IIFE and switches the API key to an env var. Will push link in a sec.

anshuman (docs): Do we prefer async IIFE or top-level await in examples? Top-level is nicer for brevity but brittle for older node toolchains.

jamal (devex): I vote IIFE for now — safest for most users. Maybe add a short comment that TLA works in modern Node/ESM.

anshuman (docs): Agreed. I'll update the template generator too so future quickstarts don't regress. Also adding a tiny note about the env var name to the onboarding checklist.

sasha (DevEx): Proposed corrected snippet pasted here:
```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
(async () => {
  const resp = await client.generate({ model: 'rw1' });
  console.log(resp);
})();
```

sasha (DevEx): And alternate TLA version for README if we ever switch:
```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
const resp = await client.generate({ model: 'rw1' });
console.log(resp);
```

docs-bot: Auto-PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4321 (fix: node quickstart example + env var) :white_check_mark:

liam (eng): Nice. Can someone add a CI smoke check that runs the codeblocks from the README (or at least the node ones)? We keep getting these.

anshuman (docs): Will add a follow-up issue + tiny CI job. Might be flaky but we can gate it to run in the docs pipeline.

jamal (devex): Thanks for catching this, @sasha. Assigning follow-up to @anshuman to update templates and add the CI check.

sasha (DevEx): Thanks all. I'll update the changelog entry for the quickstart docs and mark the onboarding task done.

liam (eng): :thumbsup:
